 750-800, not 100

Frank, 2026-09-01: "call scoring is not 0-100, they say a perfect call is
750-800." Nothing in the repo recorded the scale, so a session reading only the
numbers infers a 0-100 percentage, sees 224 and 148, and reports a scale bug
that does not exist. That is exactly what happened tonight.

No runtime change -- and worth stating why, because the obvious worry is that
something has been thresholding a 0-800 value against 100:

* `COACH_BAR_RANGES` was already empirical, (38, 251) fitted to observed
  per-producer extremes. It never assumed a 0-100 range.
* `panels.leaderboard` RANKS producers on Avg Call Score and awards places, so
  the points are scale-invariant.

So the figures and the points are all correct as shipped. What is now known to
mislead is the bar itself: with the ceiling at 251, Lorena's 224 draws nearly
full while sitting under a third of a perfect call. Re-anchoring to 800 is
honest but returns to the sliver problem the empirical range was chosen to
avoid, so this is documented and left alone rather than changed unilaterally.

Also recorded, because they bear on how much weight these numbers can take:
the per-user rows are call-weighted over Coach's own Total Calls and roll up
exactly to the team figure (12,835/142 = 90.4 vs 90; role play 399/5 = 79.8 vs
80), and Total Calls includes voicemails while Coach's coverage of a day swings
from 9 of 52 dials to 35 of 40 between producers.

