Subject: [PATCH 04/11] Coach AI scores voicemails as calls -- confirmed, and
 it explains the low averages

Frank read three of Sarahi's calls off TRAQ directly, 2026-09-01, choosing calls
by TRAQ's own labelling of the call type:

    voicemail -> score 3,   sentiment 0
    voicemail -> score 3,   sentiment 0
    live call -> score 292, sentiment 48

So a voicemail scores ~3 against a real conversation's ~292, and voicemail
sentiment is a flat 0. Avg Call Score and Avg Sentiment are answer-rate-weighted,
not call-quality measures: more voicemails reached -> lower average, independent
of how the producer actually talks. Sarahi's 25 voicemails of 35 rows are the
whole reason she posts 11.

Bearing on the leaderboard (panels.leaderboard): Avg Call Score and Avg
Sentiment each award 5/4/3/2/1. Ranking producers on a number driven by their
answer rate rewards NOT connecting -- on 2026-08-31 Lorena took first on Avg
Call Score (224) with Coach seeing only 9 of her 52 dials, because the calls she
abandons never record and never reach TRAQ, leaving only her best conversations
in the denominator. Recommend pulling both categories from the points until they
can be normalised; documented here, not changed in this commit.

No code change. TRAQ notes carry the call id, so the 2026-09-15 API key lets us
join real per-call scores onto our own live/voicemail split and drop the
inference entirely.

