Subject: [PATCH 07/11] Make the regression suite actually run: commit the
 fixtures

The suite has never run on the nightly server, and nobody knew.

tests_live_contact.py opened data/transcripts_2026-08-27.json and called
day_calls.classify() live. data/ is gitignored, so on the fresh clone the
scheduled task makes every night, it raised FileNotFoundError on line 14 before
executing a single case. The task then reported a check that had not happened.
It only ever passed in a container that had already built 2026-08-27 by hand --
which the nightly container never is.

capture_fixtures.py freezes everything is_live() needs -- the evidence dict,
talk seconds, transcript class, longest live recording -- into
fixtures/live_contact_<day>.json, which IS committed. 194 cases from 2026-08-31,
105 KB. The suite now reads that and calls the real decision function with no
network and no cached pulls. Verified by copying only fixtures/ and the .py
files into an empty directory with no data/ at all: 144 passed.

Adjudication is explicit. `expected` true/false is a ruling and a mismatch fails
the run. `expected: null` is unadjudicated -- reported every run, never failed,
so a case nobody has ruled on can never masquerade as a pass. 144 are locked in:
every case where the recording and the code already agree, which is the set the
audio settles on its own.

The remaining 50 are unadjudicated on purpose, and 6 of them are the ones that
matter -- rows where the RECORDING SAYS VOICEMAIL AND THE CODE SAYS LIVE:

    Coral   / Ricardo Vazquez           7s   "Rec Engine requesting to win back home"
    Crystal / Hector Altamirano        38s   note describes an earlier conversation
    Mike    / Elizabeth Benitez Flores 27s   "has not been interested for a while."
    Mike    / Marty Tissaw             15s   "Claims not to have a car..."
    Sarahi  / Randy Webster            28s   note describes a brush-off; audio is a screener
    Sarahi  / Thomas Runyons           13s   a to-do written before the call

Frank reported these independently: "a bunch of voicemails or no answers made it
to the 8/31 live contact stats". A seventh, Sarahi / Claudia Pineda ("phone seems
to be disconected"), has no transcript at all and so is not in this group.

NO LOGIC IS CHANGED HERE. This commit only makes the suite capable of running,
which is the prerequisite for changing is_live at all.

