From 5a1ae2c31a38663fe42eb2b89e51e87cd02312a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Flores Digest Automation <frank@floresinsuranceagency.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 09:04:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/11] Stop notes promoting a dial the recording proves was a
 voicemail

Frank, 2026-08-31: "a bunch of voicemails or no answers made it to the 8/31 live
contact stats". Five did.

The "notes win over the recording" rule (Frank, 2026-08-18) was built for one
direction: a producer writing "no answer" outranks a 12-second transcript that
sounds live. It was firing in reverse. Any note that merely LOOKED like an
outcome promoted a dial whose audio was plainly a machine greeting.

New gate: if every dial to that number that day was RECORDED and every recording
is a voicemail or no-answer, nothing promotes it. Not a weak note, not an
asserting one. The reasoning is that there is no unobserved call left for a
conversation to have happened on -- so a note claiming one is about another day,
another person, or is not the producer's words at all.

It has to outrank `asserted`, and Hector Altamirano is why. On 2026-08-31 the
lead's spouse TEXTED at 10:01 ("He didn't say he wanted to switch after i showed
him the quote"); Crystal dialled at 14:39 and got voicemail; at 15:28 she moved
the lead to Smart-Cycle and PASTED THE CUSTOMER'S TEXT into the stage-move
comment. asserts_contact then read the customer's own words as Crystal reporting
a conversation. No wording filter catches that reliably. The audio does.

SCREENERS ARE EXEMPT, and that exemption is what makes this safe. The
transcriber labels a call by how it opens, so an answering service reads as
voicemail even when a person joins. Sarahi / Randy Webster is exactly that --
classed voicemail, and the tape runs "...I'll see if this person is available.
Hello, this is from Farmers Insurance. How are you doing today? WHAT DO YOU
WANT?" That is Randy, matching her note word for word. He stays live. Measured
on 2026-08-31, ~3% of voicemail-classed calls are conversations behind a
screener and they are the only systematic false negative this gate can produce.
It also needs EVERY dial recorded: one unrecorded dial means the conversation
could have happened off-tape, and the note is then the only witness and wins.

Dropped, all confirmed with Frank:
  Coral   / Ricardo Vazquez           "Rec Engine requesting to win back home"
  Crystal / Hector Altamirano         the pasted customer text above
  Mike    / Elizabeth Benitez Flores  a month's summary, written on a voicemail day
  Mike    / Marty Tissaw              info from a 2026-02-03 note Mike echoed;
                                      he has dialled her once, ever
  Sarahi  / Thomas Runyons            a to-do written before the call

Effect on 2026-08-31: team 32 -> 27 live, 16.6% -> 14.0%. Crystal 4->3,
Mike 12->10, Coral 5->4, Sarahi 8->7, Lorena unchanged.

All 144 previously locked fixtures still pass; the six above are now adjudicated
and locked too, so 150 pass and any change that resurrects this fails the run.

STILL OPEN: Sarahi / Claudia Pineda. Her note says "phone seems to be
disconected i emailed her to contact us" -- an explicit statement of NO contact
that the negative detector misses. Her dial was unrecorded so this gate cannot
reach it. Separate fix.

