From 4c06c395319b54f05c408290b56cd69725b95519 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Flores Digest Automation <frank@floresinsuranceagency.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 17:29:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/11] Claudia Pineda: "disconected" with one n slipped the
 no-contact detector

Frank, 2026-09-01: "claudia pineda was a no contact."

Sarahi wrote "phone seems to be disconected i emailed her to contact us" -- an
explicit statement that nobody was reached -- and it scored as a live contact.
NEGATIVE matched the exact spelling `disconnected` and nothing else, so one
missing n turned a no-contact note into a contact. Now `disconn?ect(ed)?`.
These notes are typed fast between dials; spelling is not evidence of anything.

Her dial was unrecorded, which is why the machine-only gate could not reach her:
that gate deliberately requires every dial to be on tape.

Also fixes a bug I introduced in the leaderboard footnote. It read "shown in
Coaching &amp; Call Quality", and render_report locates panels with
html.find(heading) -- first literal match wins. The footnote sits earlier in the
document than the panel it named, so the build walked div depth from the
Leaderboard's opening tag and died with "panel close not found: Coaching &amp;
Call Quality". Reworded to "shown below", with a comment saying why body copy
must never repeat a panel heading verbatim.

Verified by a full rebuild of 2026-08-31 (--no-send):
  Crystal 4->3   Lorena 3->3   Mike 12->10   Coral 5->4   Sarahi 8->6
  TEAM    32->26 live, 16.6% -> 13.5%
Households quoted, premium quoted, premium sold and policy count all unchanged,
which is the expected blast radius: this touches contact classification only.

Mike's 10 still carries the separate Nicole Santana double-count (one lead
reached on two numbers, collapsed in Call Detail but not in the live count), so
the true figure is 25 and 13.0% once that lands.

151 fixtures pass.

