From e190e1cd2adaf750a3a3df99a9a4ec2ffef5dfa8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Flores Digest Automation <frank@floresinsuranceagency.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 17:43:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] One account, one contact -- even when it is reached on
 two numbers

Frank, 2026-09-01: "can we make a rule for same accounts to not count as a
duplicate even if its from another number, to avoid this duplicate situation."

`_one_row_per_lead` collapsed Call Detail but nothing else. The live count and
the contact rate come off `dials_kept`, which was never collapsed, so one human
reached on two of their own numbers scored as two contacts. Mike / Nicole
Santana on 2026-08-31: 252s on +1 917-804-1091 and 67s on +1 631-276-3801, one
lead (42759342), counted twice. His Call Detail panel showed 11 rows under a
headline of 12, which is how it surfaced. Roger Ryan was the same shape on
08-28 -- "he was already there".

The shorter dial is now marked `dropped`, reusing the mechanism the
service/renewal read already uses: finalize._totals filters dropped dials before
computing ANY figure, so the duplicate leaves the numerator and the denominator
together. That is deliberate. It is one attempt at one person, and reaching
somebody on their mobile after their landline should not read as a 50% contact
rate.

verify_finalize.py now reports ALL SIX FIGURES RECONCILE for 2026-08-31. It was
carrying three Mike mismatches -- live 12 vs 11, contact_rate 22.2 vs 20.4,
live_bucket 12 vs 11 -- every one of them this bug. That is the independent
check, not my arithmetic.

Full effect on 2026-08-31, both fixes together:
                     calls   live    rate
  as sent              193     32   16.6%
  + voicemail gate     193     26   13.5%
